# Helix workflow

One outcome per task. Default coding mode: ponytail (see `AGENTS.md`). Policy edits only in `AGENTS.md`.

## Loop

```
pull → set mode → one slice → test → commit (if asked) → next
```

1. Understand the flow before editing.
2. Change the shared call site; fewest files.
3. After logic changes: `npm run test`. Before large wrap-up: `npm run build`.
4. Commit / push / PR only when the user asks.

## Harness

| Need | Where |
|------|--------|
| Helix policy | `AGENTS.md` |
| Project skills | `.agents/skills/` |
| Personal cross-repo | Cursor User Rules / `~/.claude/skills/` |

Do not put Helix policy in `.claude/` (local/gitignored).

## DB / Supabase

Schema/migration → types/client → UI. Use project skills `supabase` and `supabase-postgres-best-practices` when touching SQL, RLS, indexes, or pooling.

## Modes

- Decisions / grilling: `/grill-me` — normal prose, no caveman.
- Heavy visual/3D: ask once whether to `stop ponytail`, then honor it.
- Reset: `normal mode` / `stop caveman` / `stop ponytail`.

## Theme

- Login: always dark (Beams). Do not wire to ThemeProvider.
- Authenticated app: `light` → `dark` → `system` via header cycle. Prefer CSS tokens (`bg-background`, etc.).

## Layout

See `.cursor/rules/helix-layout.mdc`. Phone/tablet = bottom tabs; desktop `lg+` = sidebar. Content column `max-w-6xl`.

## Done check

- Know what `git status` still has.
- No accidental `.env` or `.claude/` dumps in commits.
